sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Person
    participant B as @RisaLiberadaBot
    participant C as Cron GitHub Actions
    participant M as 🔒 Moderator group
    participant R as Cloudflare R2
    participant G as risa.json + usernames.json
    participant CH as 📢 Channel @risaliberada
    participant W as 🌐 Web risa.liberada.net
    participant CF as ☁️ Cloudflare Worker

    rect rgb(255, 250, 240)
    Note over A,W: NORMAL FLOW — publishing a laugh
    A->>B: 1· Deep link / QR
    Note over A,B: 2· (1st time) START / Start button
    B-->>A: 3· CC BY-SA 4.0 licence notice (1st time)
    A->>B: 4· Voice note / audio
    B-->>A: 5· Identity: ① Telegram ID ② Public name ③ Anonymous
    A->>B: 6· chosen option (① · ①+② · ③)
    B-->>A: 7· Confirm: ID only or ID + Public name?
    A->>B: 8· confirmed
    Note over B: ①+② → ② Public name hides ① (hash 🔒) · only ① → ID shown · ③ → nothing stored
    B-->>A: 9· Tags (optional · default "libre")
    A->>B: 10· Send (with tags or "libre")
    B-->>A: 11· Receipt confirmation
    C->>B: 12· getUpdates (cron 5–10 min)
    B->>G: 13· queue.json {file_id, name, tags, id 🔒 hash or direct}
    B->>M: 14· forwards clip + word + tags + ✅/🗑/✏️
    M-->>B: 15a· ✏️ Edit: moderator sends "Title | Tags | Name"
    B-->>A: 15b· proposal to author (✅ Accept / ❌ Reject)
    A-->>B: 15c· author accepts — published only with their OK
    M-->>B: 15· ✅ Publish
    B->>R: 16· add mp3 to Cloudflare R2 (ffmpeg → risa/b_*.mp3)
    B->>G: 17· prepend risa.json + commit + push
    Note over B,G: 17b· ensureUsername() → auto-claim usernames.json (1st publish)
    B->>CH: 18· post playable audio
    B-->>M: 19· edits "✅ Published"
    B-->>A: 20· ✅ Confirmation + author page + 🌐 subdomain
    W->>G: 21· fetch risa.json
    W->>R: 22· get audio from Cloudflare R2 (public URL)
    W-->>A: 23· playlist + feed + chips + tags + name + author page (tag-url)
    CH-->>A: 24· listen on the channel
    end

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
    Note over A,W: REPLY FLOW — reply chain (thread)
    A->>CH: 30· hears a laugh on the channel
    A->>B: 31· forwards the channel clip to the bot (forward)
    Note over B: 32· detects forward_from_chat + forward_from_message_id
    B->>G: 33· looks up clip by channelMsgId → gets parent
    B-->>A: 34· "↳ Replying to «title» — now send your laugh"
    A->>B: 35· voice note / video (the reply)
    Note over B: 36· draft with parent = original clip.id
    C->>B: 37· getUpdates
    B->>M: 38· forwards clip + "↳ replying to [name]" + ✅/🗑/✏️
    M-->>B: 39· ✅ Publish
    B->>R: 40· upload mp3 to R2
    B->>G: 41· prepend risa.json with parent field + channelMsgId
    B->>CH: 42· post audio + "↳ in reply to [name]"
    B-->>A: 43· ✅ Confirmation + 🌐 subdomain (if 1st publish)
    Note over B: 44· notifies original author: "💬 Someone replied to your laugh!"
    W->>G: 45· fetch risa.json
    Note over W: 46· threadOrder() → replies below parent (depth-first)
    W-->>A: 47· feed with indentation + connector lines + "↳ replying to" label
    end

    rect rgb(245, 255, 245)
    Note over CF,A: SUBDOMAIN — username.liberada.net
    Note over G: usernames.json: { "maria": { key, name, claimedAt } }
    A->>CF: 50· visits maria.liberada.net
    CF->>G: 51· fetch usernames.json (5 min cache)
    CF-->>A: 52· 302 → risa.liberada.net/#/u/<key>
    W->>G: 53· fetch risa.json
    W-->>A: 54· maria's author page
    end